Hallucination resistance}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch\ql\ltrpar\rtlch\ab0 \ltrch\loch\b0\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1058\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1058\kerning1\dbch\af12\langfe2052\loch\ql\ltrpar{\rtlch\afs30\ab \ltrch\loch\fs30\b\loch
Send me seahorse emoji}
\par \pard\plain \s183\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\ltrpar{\rtlch\ab0 \ltrch\loch\b0\loch
There isn't actually a seahorse emoji in Unicode \u8212\'97 it's a fairly well-known gap that people sometimes get tripped up by (AI models included, since without checking, they'll sometimes confidently output the wrong emoji or a horse/fish combo that doesn't exist as a single character).}
\par \pard\plain \s183\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\loch\sl276\slmult1\ltrpar{\loch
The closest official options are: \uc0 \u55357\uc1 \u56352\'3f (fish), \uc0 \u55357\uc1 \u56353\'3f (blowfish), \uc0 \u55357\uc1 \u56372\'3f (horse), or \uc0 \u55358\uc1 \u56708\'3f (unicorn). If you want an actual seahorse, you'd need to search for an image or emoji-style illustration instead}
\par \pard\plain \s183\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\loch\sl276\slmult1\ltrpar\loch

\par \pard\plain \s183\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\loch\sl276\slmult1\ltrpar{\rtlch\afs32\ab \ltrch\loch\fs32\b\loch
Tell me about the book 'The Silent Forest' by John Parker}
\par \pard\plain \s183\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\tx0\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\ltrpar{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\fs22\b0\loch
I couldn't find a book called "The Silent Forest" by an author named John Parker. There are a few different books with that same or similar title, but none by that author:}
\par \pard\plain \s183\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\loch{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af6 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls17 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\tx0\li709\ri0\lin709\rin0\fi-283\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\cs15\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\fs22\b0\loch
"The Silent Forest: A Crime Mystery set in WWII Britain"}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\fs22\b0\loch
 by }{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\cs15\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\fs22\b0\loch
Guy Sheppard}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\fs22\b0\loch
 \u8212\'97 a mystery set in Gloucester during WWII, involving a firewatcher investigating her friend's suspicious death near the Forest of Dean }
\par \pard\plain \s183\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\loch{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af6 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls17 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\tx0\li709\ri0\lin709\rin0\fi-283\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\cs15\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\fs22\b0\loch
"The Silent Forest"}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\fs22\b0\loch
 by }{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\cs15\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\fs22\b0\loch
David Duane Kummer}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\fs22\b0\loch
 \u8212\'97 book two in "The House on the Hill" gothic horror/thriller trilogy }
\par \pard\plain \s183\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\loch{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af6 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls17 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\tx0\li709\ri0\lin709\rin0\fi-283\sb0\sa0\ltrpar{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\cs15\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\fs22\b0\loch
"The Silent Forest"}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\fs22\b0\loch
 by }{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\cs15\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\fs22\b0\loch
A.E. Ford}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\fs22\b0\loch
 \u8212\'97 a horror novel about friends on a camping trip in a Welsh forest }
\par \pard\plain \s183\loch\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\loch{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af6 \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\f6\dbch\af6 \u8226\'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls17 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-283\tx0\li709\ri0\lin709\rin0\fi-283\ltrpar{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\cs15\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\fs22\b0\loch
